## Requirements

- Java 21
- Node.js 22+

## Getting started

Install the frontend dependencies first:

```bash
npm --prefix frontend install
```

{{- if eq .database "postgres" }}

Start PostgreSQL:

```bash
docker compose up -d db
```

{{- end }}

Run the API:

```bash
mvn spring-boot:run
```

In another terminal, run the frontend:

```bash
npm --prefix frontend run dev
```

The API listens on <http://localhost:8080> and the frontend on
<http://localhost:5173>. Vite proxies `/api` requests to the backend.

## API

- `GET /api/health` returns `{"status":"ok"}`.
- `GET /api/items` lists items.
- `POST /api/items` creates an item with `{"name":"First item"}`.
- `GET /api/items/{id}` returns one item.
- `DELETE /api/items/{id}` deletes an item.

{{- if eq .database "h2" }}

The H2 console is available at <http://localhost:8080/h2-console> while the
application is running. Use the JDBC URL shown in `application.yml`.

{{- else }}

PostgreSQL connection settings are read from `.env` or from environment
variables: `SPRING_DATASOURCE_URL`, `SPRING_DATASOURCE_USERNAME` and
`SPRING_DATASOURCE_PASSWORD`.

{{- end }}

## Tests

```bash
mvn test
```

The test profile uses an in-memory H2 database, even when the application runs
with PostgreSQL.

{{- if has .tools "docker" }}

## Docker

Build and run both services with Docker Compose:

```bash
docker compose up --build
```

{{- end }}

